  "_comment": "Curated per-product tablet/capsule strengths — the strengths a branded fixed-dose medication actually ships in, so a logged brand ('Concerta') can be logged as a *pill* (tap 36 mg → '1 tablet · 36 mg') instead of typing raw milligrams. DISPLAY/ENTRY CONVENIENCE ONLY: a chip selects the dose `amount` (strength × count) and nothing else — it drives no pharmacology, no PSID identity, no dose ladder, and no curve, exactly like the alcohol by-volume logger picks grams. Consumed by sqlite.py build_product_strengths() → the `product_strengths` table, read by SubstanceStore.productStrengths(forProduct:). Every `product` must already exist as a brand alias of its `parent` (the same coverage gate release-families/brands.json use); a miss is reported by the build, not failed, since available aliases vary by build. Scope is deliberately the ADHD/adjacent stimulant + non-stimulant formulations the med-manager audience takes daily (Specs/adhd-audience-fit); extend as other branded fixed-strength products earn it. Strengths are FDA prescribing information (DailyMed), ascending, in milligrams; `form` is 'tablet' or 'capsule' (the count noun). Liquid/patch/ODT products are intentionally omitted until their unit is modeled.",
